#
# === LEDGER CONTEXT (from W44-146 refresh, 4f2b1573) ===
#
# Photo cluster: 375 cells (5 images × 5 efforts × 15 distances)
# Mean SSIM2 delta vs cjxl: -0.392 (FLAT across W110/W134/W141/W146,
#   spanning 4 ledger refreshes without movement)
#
# Per-image (mean SSIM2 delta, worst SSIM2 delta):
#   1025469.png   -0.353  -1.00  (closest to parity, 75 cells)
#   1189261.png   -0.068  -1.12  (W44-91 closed the worst cells)
#   1418519.png   -0.565  -2.57  (WORST, no current sub-gate)
#   1420710.png   -0.460  -2.13  (W44-96/98 covers but residual at d=6)
#   1531677.png   -0.513  -2.00  (W44-96/99/100 covers but residual at d=3-6)
#
# Per-distance (all 25 cells per d):
#   d <= 0.6: mean -0.02 to -0.05 (at parity)
#   d 0.8-2.5: mean -0.09 to -0.32 (mild deficit)
#   d 3.0-6.0: mean -0.79 to -1.24 (MAJOR deficit, target band)
#
# === TOP 10 PHOTO CELLS BY SSIM2 DEFICIT ===
#
# 1418519 cluster (6 of 10):
#   e8 d=5 -2.57   e9 d=5 -2.57   e7 d=5 -2.39
#   e7 d=6 -2.30   e8 d=6 -2.17   e9 d=6 -2.17
# 1420710 cluster (4 of 10):
#   e8 d=6 -2.13   e9 d=6 -2.13   e6 d=6 -2.12   e7 d=6 -2.11
#
# === TOP 10 PHOTO CELLS AT-PARITY-BYTES (|bytes| <= 1%) ===
# (Most actionable — SSIM2 win not gated by bytes wedge)
#
# 1531677 e7 d=5 -2.00 +0.53%   1531677 e8 d=6 -1.70 +0.35%
# 1531677 e9 d=6 -1.70 +0.58%   1531677 e8 d=5 -1.43 -0.10%
# 1531677 e9 d=5 -1.43 +0.50%   1531677 e5 d=3 -1.32 -0.32%
# 1531677 e6 d=3 -1.17 -0.98%   1531677 e5 d=4 -1.17 -0.74%
# 1189261 e9 d=6 -1.12 +0.22%   1420710 e7 d=3 -1.09 -0.17%
#
# 1531677 dominates the actionable list — 8 of 10.
#
# === PER-CELL MECHANISM (5 cells dumped) ===
#
# Cell                  | Agreement | Δ_fb   | Δ_Y    | Mechanism class
# ---                   | ---       | ---    | ---    | ---
# 1418519 e8 d=5        | 98.8%     | 0/317  | +9     | A (downstream/recon)
# 1418519 e7 d=5        | 98.8%     | 0/317  | +38    | A (downstream/recon)
# 1531677 e7 d=5        | 86.9%     | -92/433| +225   | B (DCT32X32 over-pick)
# 1420710 e8 d=6        | 88.4%     | -55/348| +94    | B (DCT32X32 over-pick)
# 1531677 e5 d=3        | 70.7%     | -622/1195| -1502| C (DCT32+ massive over-pick @ low effort)
#
# === MECHANISM A — 1418519 d=5/6 (recon/EPF divergence) ===
#
# Per-strategy first-block counts byte-IDENTICAL between ours and cjxl
# at every effort tested (e7, e8). Y-channel nonzero deltas tiny (+9
# at e8, +38 at e7). Per-region mean qac matches cjxl to within 0.1.
# The 1.2% non-agreement cells are at the DCT32X64 vs DCT64X32 vs
# DCT32X32 boundary — minor strategy oscillations on identical Y energy.
#
# This MATCHES W44-138 Phase 1's finding (+0.034 R max-abs at after_epf
# on 1418519 d=5 e8) and W44-139's verdict (SSIM2-neutral in production
# because W44-118 hard-gates W44-117 OFF on photos). The bytes-identical
# strategy + tokens explains why W44-91/96/98/99 stack cannot help —
# those gates change entropy_mul / DCT lift to shift strategy selection,
# but here selection is already at parity.
#
# 1418519 has mask=76 (W44-118 PROBE output), m3=23, fcbr=0.05 — fails
# both W44-29 mask<50 gate AND W44-91 m3>=80 gate AND W44-96 ed>=0.7
# gate. **No current sub-discriminator admits 1418519.**
#
# Phase 2 fix for A: needs measurement-only photo-class W44-117 gate
# (separate from the W44-118 `is_screenshot` mask). W44-139 already
# scoped this as a measurement chunk; recommendation is to expand the
# W44-139 cell set (4 → 25+ cells, all 1418519 d>=3 plus other photos)
# AND ADD a measurement-only env-var hook (`JXL_W44_118_SCREENSHOT_ONLY=0`
# or equivalent) to actually fire W44-117 on photos and measure SSIM2.
# Risk: 1025469 e8/e9 d=4 -0.85 SSIM2 regression (the original W44-118
# fix); but 1025469 mask=76.08 ≈ 1418519 mask=76 — they likely behave
# the same way. If both go down, abandon. If 1418519 goes UP and 1025469
# down by <+0.85, may need finer discriminator.
#
# === MECHANISM B — 1420710/1531677 d=5/6 (DCT32X32 over-pick) ===
#
# Top disagreement pairs (1531677 e7 d=5, 86.9% agreement):
#   DCT32X32 → DCT16X32  96 cells  (we pick larger, cjxl picks smaller)
#   DCT32X32 → DCT16X16  80 cells
#   DCT32X16 → DCT16X16  76 cells
#   DCT32X16 → DCT32X32  56 cells
#   DCT32X32 → DCT32X16  48 cells  (oscillation between rectangular)
#   DCT32X16 → DCT16X8   28 cells
#
# Top disagreement pairs (1420710 e8 d=6, 88.4% agreement):
#   DCT32X32 → DCT32X16  208 cells  (very large skew)
#   DCT32X32 → DCT16X32  128 cells
#   DCT32X32 → DCT16X16  96 cells
#   DCT32X32 → DCT8X16   10 cells
#
# In both cells we pick DCT32X32 where cjxl picks DCT32X16 / DCT16X32 /
# DCT16X16. Total first-block count delta: ours 341 vs cjxl 433 on
# 1531677 (we use 92 fewer blocks total because each block is larger);
# 293 vs 348 on 1420710 (55 fewer blocks). Y-channel total token delta
# is small (+225 and +94) — so the bytes savings come from fewer blocks,
# the SSIM2 loss comes from larger blocks blurring high-frequency
# detail in textured photo regions.
#
# **W44-96/98/99/100 LIFT dct32x32 entropy_mul ABOVE the default for
# these images, but per-table inspection shows the lift is for the
# OPPOSITE direction**: variant Z (W44-96) raises dct32x32 from 1.34
# default to 1.20 (LOWER number = SMALLER cost penalty = MORE picks of
# DCT32X32). So we EXPLICITLY made DCT32X32 cheaper on 1420710/1531677,
# and the W44-147 dumps show it's now too cheap at d=5/6/e5-e9.
#
# The W44-98 / W44-99 measurement DID see this at certain (e, d) cells
# but did NOT cover d=5/6 across e5-e9; the wins were measured on
# d=5 e8/e9 (W44-98) and d=5 e8/e9 (W44-99). The wider sweep was never
# done. W44-100 micro-bisected dct16x32 to 1.23 (LOW colour table) but
# never re-checked dct32x32.
#
# Phase 2 fix for B: REVISIT variant Z's dct32x32 lift on 1420710 +
# 1531677 across the d=3-6 × e5-e9 grid. Bisect dct32x32 values
# {1.20, 1.24, 1.28, 1.34} to find pareto-optimal per-image (the
# W44-98/99 split already exists). This may CLOSE the d=5/6 deficit
# at cost of LOSING the original W44-98/99 d=5 e8/e9 wins (need to
# verify with measurement). Risk: low-medium (the gates exist; we're
# tuning a single number within a narrow range).
#
# === MECHANISM C — 1531677 e5 d=3 (DCT32+ massive over-pick) ===
#
# Strategy agreement 70.7%. cjxl picks ~3× more first-blocks total
# (1195 vs 573) AND emits more Y tokens (44217 vs 42715). Top
# disagreement: DCT32X32 → DCT8 (252 cells), DCT32X16 → DCT8 (123),
# DCT16X32 → DCT8 (111) — we pick LARGE transforms where cjxl picks
# the smallest. We also pick DCT16X32 / DCT32X16 where cjxl picks
# DCT16X8 / DCT8X16 / DCT8.
#
# This is the SAME shape as B but more severe — at e5 the cost model
# has less iterations to refine, and the W44-29 + W44-96/99 lift stack
# is firing harder (variant Z at low effort = aggressive DCT32X32
# admission). 1531677 e5 d=3 fires W44-29 (mask 35.63 < 50, d>=3 ✓),
# fires W44-91 if m3>=80 (no — 1531677 m3=12.30 → fails), fires W44-96
# (d>=4.5 — NO, d=3 fails the inner gate). So at e5 d=3 only W44-29
# fires; the dct32x32 entropy_mul comes from the OUTER suppressed table
# (1.34 default → suppressed_default 1.34, still LOWER cost = MORE
# DCT32X32 admission).
#
# 1531677 e5 d=3 fails the W44-96 gate (d>=4.5) so doesn't use variant
# Z. At d=4 it would still fail (just barely). At d=4.5+ it kicks in.
# So 1531677 e5 d=3 / d=4 cells use the outer W44-29 table.
#
# Phase 2 fix for C: separate from B. The W44-29 OUTER table may be
# too aggressive on 1531677-class at d=3 e5/e6. New sub-discriminator
# OR distance-band split. Per-cell EV: 2 cells (e5/e6 d=3, e5/e6 d=4
# both still W44-29 outer), SSIM2 -1.32 and -1.17 (medium impact).
#
# === ACTIONABLE PHASE 2 CANDIDATES (RANKED) ===
#
# 1. MECHANISM B (variant Z dct32x32 d=5/6 bisect on 1420710/1531677)
#    - EV: HIGH — closes 8 of 10 photo at-parity-bytes top cells
#    - Risk: MEDIUM — may sacrifice W44-98/99 e8/e9 d=5 wins
#    - Effort: 2-3d (bisect + verify W44-98/99 cells stay FIXED)
#    - Cells closed: 1531677 e5/e6/e7/e8/e9 d=5/6, 1420710 e6/e7/e8/e9 d=6
#      (up to ~14 cells; SSIM2 wins +0.5 to +2.0 expected)
#
# 2. MECHANISM A (photo W44-117 admission with new discriminator)
#    - EV: MED-HIGH — closes 6 of 10 SSIM2-deficit top cells
#    - Risk: HIGH — 1025469-class regressions (W44-118 precedent)
#    - Effort: 1d measurement (env-var hook + sweep), then 2-3d if
#      results pareto-positive
#    - Cells closed: 1418519 e7/e8/e9 d=5/6 (up to 6 cells)
#    - Pre-requisite: lift the W44-118 hard gate to admit
#      photo-class mask~76 path (NEW: m3<25 OR ed<X discriminator)
#
# 3. MECHANISM C (W44-29 outer table d=3 e5/e6 on 1531677-class)
#    - EV: LOW-MED — closes 2-4 cells
#    - Risk: LOW — narrow targeted fix, easy to gate to 1531677 only
#    - Effort: 1d
#    - Cells closed: 1531677 e5/e6 d=3 (and possibly d=4)
#
# === RECOMMENDATION: spawn W44-148 as Mechanism B bisect ===
#
# Highest EV/risk ratio. Pre-existing W44-98/99 infrastructure means
# the gate already exists — the only change is the dct32x32 number
# in the variant Z tables. Bisect runs in ~1h paired interleaved A/B
# on 14 target cells × 5 variants. If pareto-optimal value exists
# (likely — W44-77 already proved this kind of bisect works), ship as
# 1-line constant change (W44-98 high-colour table + W44-99/100 LOW
# colour table). If no pareto-optimal value, HONEST-STOP and try
# Mechanism A as W44-149.
#
# === DO NOT (binding for future agents) ===
#
# 1. DO NOT re-investigate Mechanism A without first ENLARGING the
#    W44-139 cell set (4 → 25+) AND adding a measurement-only gate-
#    bypass env-var. W44-139 explicitly scoped this as 1-day measurement
#    work; respawning the same 4-cell experiment will produce the same
#    SSIM2-zero result.
#
# 2. DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for any photo cluster SSIM2 gap (per
#    W44-66 user correction).
#
# 3. DO NOT respawn the per-block adaptive qac approach (W44-145
#    HONEST-STOPPED at e5-e7 because cjxl runs FLAT qac there). On
#    photos at e5 d=3 the W44-147 dump shows per-region qac is at parity
#    — qac is NOT the lever; strategy selection is.
#
# 4. DO NOT widen variant Z dct32x32 BELOW 1.20 — Mechanism B fix needs
#    to RAISE the number (1.20 → 1.24+) so DCT32X32 is MORE expensive
#    and we pick DCT16X16 / DCT32X16 / DCT16X32 instead. Lowering would
#    make the problem worse.
#
# 5. DO NOT remove or weaken W44-118's is_screenshot gate without a
#    measurement-validated photo discriminator. The W44-118 was a
#    fix for a -0.85 SSIM2 regression on 1025469; removing the gate
#    risks re-introducing that regression on 1025469-class photos that
#    sit close to (mask 76, similar to 1418519's mask 76).
#
# 6. DO NOT spawn a W44-29 outer-table bisect (Mechanism C) before
#    closing B. C only covers 2-4 cells and the bisect surface is much
#    smaller — wait for B's outcome to inform whether the W44-29 outer
#    table needs revisiting at all.
